  "concepts.json: three entries inserted (gen_frozen_peaks, gen_powder_snow, gen_powder_snow_bucket) and descKo lines added to the gen_ concepts above that had none; nothing reformatted.",
  "lexicon-tags.json: three hand-written entries for the new concepts, without a curriculum band (so no never-met core word is added).",
  "lang/content/en_us.json and de_de.json: the step, finale and gloss keys of the 15 trails and the three new words.",
  "src/test/resources/content-baseline.json: gipfelwaechter, gletscherpfad and sternenhaus leave reachabilityDebt (their old steps needed Nether items); the three ids were the only change of mine, BATCH-010's removals merged cleanly.",
  "content/korean/pronunciation-review.tsv, lines.jsonl, review-status.json, docs/book/src/quest-tree.md and content/metrics-baseline.json regenerated (all metrics equal or better)."
 ],
 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "A HOLDING condition on an item without a curated concept cannot be spoken by the validator's namer (QuestlineValidationTest.everyConditionAppearsInTheKoreanClue uses Catalog.ofConcepts, so \"망원경을 들고\" counts as missing), and IconReferentTest forbids giving the spyglass a concept with its item. The spyglass trails use HOLD_WHILE (goal, no condition) instead; a HOLDING condition would need the namer to fall back on names.json.",
  "HOLD_WHILE with a WAIT inner goal cannot be driven by PlaytestTest (\"8초 남았어요\"), so the observatory finale is a night walk with the spyglass near the bricks (HOLD_WHILE with a TIME inner condition and seconds) and cannot say 기다리세요.",
  "PLACE_ON_PATTERN on a ROW prints \"세 개\" whatever the size of the built row (a four-block row gave \"자갈 세 개 옆에 …\"), so mondpfad builds a row of three.",
  "REACH_HEIGHT can only ask for a descent when the ceiling is below sea level (\"높이 62 이하로 내려가세요\"). A fall from a mountain to the surface at Y 64 or more has no goal, and nothing in the generator says 떨어지다; the fall trail's finale is authored for that reason, and its goal is only satisfiable where the terrain dips under Y 62.",
  "A SEQUENCE part does not get the taught word: \"산 위로 올라가고 가문비나무 묘목을 심으세요\" names the exact sapling while its hint says 묘목.",
  "Condition objects take the key `weather` (WEATHER) and `phase` (TIME); a WEATHER condition written with `phase` was accepted by the loader and only tools/validate_schema.py caught it.",
  "Finale uniqueness (finalTextsAndAuthoredCluesAreUnique) collides for the plainest closing lines: \"밤에 침대에서 잤어요\" (sternenpfad) and \"밤에 초를 켰어요\" (w1_01) blocked two trails, so those steps name the exact thing (주황색 침대, 하얀색 초). The generator has no way to vary a finale other than naming a variant.",
  "Pairs saturated by earlier trails and by BATCH-010 (PLACE torch, lantern and hay block, KINDLE campfire, STAND candle and oak sign, GIVE carrot, wheat and sugar to a horse, CRAFT clock, WATCH sheep and cat, GO to a river or the ocean) forced unusual picks: gravel rows, a cauldron as a trough, a jack o'lantern, a planks pillar. Seven pairs of mine now sit exactly at the limit of 3 (STAND spruce_sign, PLACE ladder, WATCH goat, PLANT lily_of_the_valley, PLACE furnace, PLACE jack_o_lantern, PLACE glass).",
  "A new word is unknown for its first three sentences, so two new words in one sentence break the \"one unknown word\" rule until one of them has been met three times. The learner path puts the adv_adventure_* trails (order 208 to 231) right after the first level-2 trails, which leaves them almost no known words; the spyglass is met three times (craft, two HOLD_WHILE steps) before the finale for that reason.",
  "HOLD_WHILE is listed as a form-dependent goal in the brief, but in code only PLACE_REL, PLACE_ON_PATTERN, GIVE and an ordered SEQUENCE are; the four HOLD_WHILE steps count as normal steps."
 ],
 "openIssues": [
  "Reachability in the first week: the spyglass needs an amethyst shard (a geode) and copper, so adv_adventure_spyglass_at_parrot is only reachable if a geode turns up near the start; the brief assumes it is. The sparse jungle (parrots), frozen peaks, snowy slopes and the grove each need a mountain or jungle region near spawn. Honey needs bees, bottles and a flower field, candles need honeycomb, the bucket of powder snow needs an iron bucket and a snowy biome.",
  "The fall finale (\"양동이를 들고 높이 62 이하로 내려가세요\") is only reachable where the surface drops under Y 62 near the player, and the sensor does not check the landing or the survival.",
  "w4_06 has no lake biome to ask for: the lake is a meadow with water beside it. Polar bears (gletscherpfad) spawn in snowy plains and ice spikes, not on the peaks, so the finale may need a walk.",
  "Three finales are authored (schneesturm, sternenhaus, fall) for the 은/는 contrast and 떨어지다. 303 of 422 finales are generated against a minimum of 296.",
  "wanderpfad keeps the exact sapling in the clue (가문비나무 묘목) while the hint says 묘목: the weakness above.",
  "The brief's 위/아래/앞/뒤 of creatures is not used: a creature as an anchor moves, so every 앞 anchor here is a facing block (door, bed, furnace).",
  "BATCH-010 landed while I worked: its two removals from reachabilityDebt and mine merged without a clash; the baseline numbers in `metrics` show all three stages."
 ]
